cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below, together with the
  upstream PyUltraLight and PyUltraLight 2 works listed under references.
type: software
title: "PyUltraLight 2, SK fork (PyUL_SK)"
abstract: >-
  Fork of PyUltraLight 2 used for the Stone Skipping black-hole simulations:
  cell-centred grids, manual dynamical friction, isolated-potential and
  portability fixes on top of the upstream split-step Schroedinger-Poisson
  solver with N-body particles.
version: "30.50"
authors:
